33:12.960 --> 33:15.580
That soil feeds the tree, allowing it to grow more leaves.

33:15.860 --> 33:17.500
The system is structurally closed.

33:17.860 --> 33:18.980
The waste is the fuel.

33:18.980 --> 33:21.780
And to measure how well a system achieves this,

33:22.380 --> 33:26.080
Flyxion introduces a metric called the order parameter lambda.

33:26.600 --> 33:30.940
This is the ultimate mathematical test of whether a technology or an infrastructure

33:30.940 --> 33:32.760
will survive long term.

33:32.980 --> 33:36.680
Lambda measures the system's dependence on outside resources per cycle.

33:37.040 --> 33:40.760
If your lambda is less than one, your system is in a contractive regime.

33:41.140 --> 33:44.880
It requires fewer exogenous resources from the outside world every cycle

33:44.880 --> 33:47.720
because it is successfully reintegrating its own waste.

33:48.220 --> 33:49.980
It is successfully xylomorphic.

33:50.460 --> 33:52.120
If lambda equals one, it's critical.

33:52.300 --> 33:54.120
It is perfectly balanced, just surviving.

33:54.680 --> 33:58.980
But if your lambda is greater than one, the system is in an expansive regime.

33:59.360 --> 34:03.520
Expansive sounds like a good business word, but in thermodynamics, it is the death sentence.

34:04.160 --> 34:06.060
An expansive system bleeds resources.

34:06.640 --> 34:09.520
It constantly demands fresh energy and fresh materials from the outside,

34:09.820 --> 34:11.700
and it throws its waste away into the void.

34:11.700 --> 34:14.500
Orbital compute-launching servers to space,

34:14.860 --> 34:17.840
radiating all that computational heat uselessly into the vacuum

34:17.840 --> 34:20.620
while requiring constant rocket launches for maintenance,

34:20.840 --> 34:23.340
is strictly a lambda greater than one system.

34:23.740 --> 34:26.380
It is mathematically guaranteed to diverge and collapse

34:26.380 --> 34:28.340
under the weight of its own scaling demands.

34:28.660 --> 34:29.200
Exactly.

34:29.500 --> 34:31.060
It's totally unsustainable.

34:31.600 --> 34:33.540
So what does this all mean for us on Earth?

